// Placeholder so the `src/` directory is tracked by git. Medusa's CLI runs
// `babel src -d dist` on boot, which fails when the directory is missing.
// Dotfiles are ignored by both babel and Medusa's module loaders, so this
// file is never compiled or loaded. Add custom backend code
// (api/, models/, services/, ...) here as needed.
//
// NOTE: do NOT add a root-level `babel.config.js` for backend sources —
// Next.js disables its SWC compiler whenever one is present and the
// storefront build breaks (`next/font` requires SWC). The empty `src/`
// compiles to zero files, so no babel config is needed until real backend
// sources exist; if that day comes, scope the config to the backend only.
